  "label": "TMUA 2019 · Paper 1 · Question 15",
  "lead": "<img class=\"source-question\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"button\" aria-label=\"Enlarge question\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"TMUA 2019 · Paper 1 · Question 15 — Find the nonzero real solution of 2^(9^x)/8^(3^x)=1/4.\">",
  "options": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C",
    "D",
    "E",
    "F"
  ],
  "correct": "A",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Simplify the nested powers",
      "body": "<p>Set <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. Then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>9</mn><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. Also rewrite the denominator base 8 as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "Name the repeated inner exponential and use one common outer base.",
      "pitfall": "The numerator is 2 raised to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi></msup></mrow></math>, not 2 multiplied by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi></msup></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Rewrite the full equation as a quotient of powers of 2.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l05",
          "reminder": "Name the repeated inner exponential and use one common outer base."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Equate the outer exponents",
      "body": "<p>The equation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. Thus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.</p>",
      "recap": "A same-base quotient subtracts exponents before they are equated.",
      "pitfall": "Keep the negative exponent when rewriting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></math>.",
      "pause": "Factor <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b1-l05",
          "reminder": "A same-base quotient subtracts exponents before they are equated."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Restore x and check the request",
      "body": "<p>Solve the quadratic and retain only roots in the positive range of the exponential. Undo the substitution for each permitted root and apply the nonzero restriction on x.</p>",
      "recap": "Substitution roots must be converted back to the original variable.",
      "pitfall": "A permitted substituted value may give an original input excluded by the question.",
      "pause": "Find every permitted root, recover x and keep the nonzero solution.",
      "recall": [
        {
          "lessonId": "p1-b3-l04",
          "reminder": "Substitution roots must be converted back to the original variable."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "solution": "<p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003E;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>, so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>9</mn><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>. The equation becomes <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mn>8</mn><mrow><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>u</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math>.</p><p>Equal powers of 2 have equal exponents, giving <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x0002B;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mi>u</mi><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>. Thus <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msup><mn>3</mn><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math> or 2, yielding <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>.</p><p>The requested real nonzero solution is <strong><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><msub><mi>log</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>, option A.</strong></p>",
